@startuml proposed_layout
salt
{
  {+ "Control Panel — PROPOSED simplified layout (wireframe, for discussion)" }
  {* File | Setup | Help }
  {
    {^"1. Configure"
      Deals: "64  " | Seat: ^S^ | Samples: "50"
      [X] biq+biq (N/S Extern)   [ ] Auto-exit at end
    }
  }
  {
    {^"2. Mode  (one selector replaces 4 scattered groups)"
      Mode: ^Whole-system (default)^
      "  └ options swap by mode: A/B (A/B), Side (Double-Pair), PBN (No-peek)"
    }
  }
  {
    {^"3. Run  (one path)"
      [ ▶ Start ]  [ ⏸ Step ▷ ]  [ ⏮ Reset ]
      "progress: ▮▮▮▮▮▯▯▯  deal 5/8"
      "● server   ● biq   ● clicker"
    }
  }
  {
    {^"4. Result"
      "M2026-..-X.qss   -341 IMP / 59 bd"
      [ Export .qss ] | [ Aggregate ] | [ ⏻ Stop + kill wine ]
    }
  }
  {
    {^"Setup menu (one-time, hidden from main view)"
      "• Calibrate server buttons"
      "• Calibrate clicker / autoplay"
      "• Launch Q-Plus  • New run (reset logs)"
    }
  }
}
note bottom
  Consolidation moves:
  1) ONE start path (Start = old "Run full session"; Step ▷ keeps the debugger).
     Delete the "Manual startup steps" trio.
  2) ONE "Mode" dropdown {Whole-system, A/B, Double-Pair, No-peek cardplay}
     replaces the four separate group boxes / sub-dialog.
  3) All CALIBRATION + housekeeping moves under a "Setup" menu — it is one-time,
     not per-run, so it should not crowd the run controls.
  This is a PROPOSAL — confirm before any code change.
end note
@enduml
